#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110754 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110456 :question/id #uuid "42313322-7535-5969-ad84-958449e48c1b" :question/math-academy-id "e-3480" :question/problem "The point $A$ is located in the first quadrant and lies on the unit circle. The $y$-coordinate of $A$ is $\\dfrac{5}{9}.$ What is the $x$-coordinate of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the point $A$ lies on the unit circle, it must satisfy the Pythagorean theorem: \n\n$$\nx^2+y^2=1 .\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y=\\dfrac{5}{9}$ into the above and solving for $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\tx^2+y^2&=1\\[5pt]\n\t        x^2+\\left(\\dfrac{5}{9}\\right)^2&=1\\[5pt]\n\t\tx^2+\\left(\\dfrac{25}{81}\\right)&=1\\[5pt]\n\t\tx^2&= 1-\\dfrac{25}{81}\\[5pt]\n\t\tx^2&= \\dfrac{56}{81}\\[5pt]\n\t\tx&= \\sqrt{\\dfrac{56}{81}}\\[5pt]\n\t        x&= \\pm \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{14}}{9}.\n}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ lies in the first quadrant, $x$ must be positive. So, we select the positive answer. \n\nTherefore, our final answer is $x=\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{14}}{9}.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87c18ea8-af12-52bd-8420-ec24ed63de65" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049224 :topic/math-academy-id 433 :topic/title "The Pythagorean Theorem"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110987 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e88fcef-2ef9-533c-a8ca-bcedb24c445f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107636} {:answer/id #uuid "b3c3d912-edb9-5612-a883-39811dac0b62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107637} {:answer/id #uuid "cea0e368-fdbb-5547-b6cd-900a17d25537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x =-\\frac{\\sqrt{31}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107638} {:answer/id #uuid "61f9b397-1a45-504c-b606-93109bc348c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/valu