he point $A$ lies on the unit circle, it must satisfy the Pythagorean theorem: \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}$ into the above and solving for $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(\\frac{5}{9}) & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1-\\frac{5}{9} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{9}} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ lies in the first quadrant, $x$ must be positive, so we select the positive answer. Therefore, our final answer is $x=\\frac{2}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259695 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e2c5600-797d-5dbf-82c6-38d1f84faa2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257030} {:answer/id #uuid "74fd787b-5a48-5721-ace4-53d2a3ae18c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257805} {:answer/id #uuid "8eaeb7d8-bab9-59df-bc4b-9bc4a2cd6abe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258039} {:answer/id #uuid "df96c081-601c-58bb-a7e3-d920b7e1b2fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258730} {:answer/id #uuid "f62bb330-cd3c-5d2d-bc3f-9d00a76f8b7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df96c081-601c-58bb-a7e3-d920b7e1b2fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258730} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae52c65d-229d-5240-a6b7-89e661e7fe0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259337}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "19802aad-5d1c-554b-bf6